# Story 95: Connecting to Upstream (50s)
# Hook: Point Rysh at a workspace URL and an API key -- now your session can join the hub.
# Duration: 50s
# Source: story-095-connecting-to-upstream.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Point Rysh at a workspace URL and an API key -- now your session can join the hub.

[00:03.0 --> 00:11.0]
Upstream lives in your rysh.config under the [upstream] section: enabled, the server url, and your api_key.

[00:11.0 --> 00:19.0]
Start rysh with --shared and it auto-shares the first pane to the workspace as soon as it boots.

[00:19.0 --> 00:28.0]
Double-Escape into rysh mode. ##upstream status shows your configuration and whether the connection is live.

[00:28.0 --> 00:38.0]
The client connects over NATS-over-WebSocket to rysh-server. ##upstream my-shares lists what this session has published.

[00:38.0 --> 00:46.0]
Prefer env vars? RYSH_UPSTREAM_ENABLED, RYSH_UPSTREAM_URL, and RYSH_UPSTREAM_API_KEY override the config at launch.

[00:46.0 --> 00:50.0]
Config or flags, you're connected to the workspace -- ready to share and subscribe.

